\subsection{Method \code{new()}}{
Initializes an \code{RSNANumber} instance that represents a scalar numeric \code{NA} value.
This class exists specifically to distinguish between regular numeric values and \code{NA},
and should be used when an \code{NA} must be explicitly wrapped in the scalar object model.

Internally, this method delegates to the parent \code{RSNumber} class,
passing \code{as.numeric(NA)} as the scalar value.
